{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DhYCHcUFnoAFTemDEvMpq5","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t  \"reason\": \"<one line>\",\n201\t  \"cumulative_evals\": 1,\n202\t  \"skills_used\": [\"KernelWiki?\"],\n203\t  \"tokens_note\": \"optional budget snapshot\"\n204\t}\n205\t```\n206\tRules: `decision` ∈ {keep, revert, iterate}; `parent` links lineage (c002.parent\n207\t= c001, etc.); fill actual speedups/margins from evaluator output; keep records\n208\timmutable once written.\n209\t\n210\t---\n211\t\n212\t## 7. Execution checklist (workflow guardrails)\n213\t\n214\t1. Consult **KernelWiki** for A800/`sm_80` RMSNorm-backward fusion + atomic /\n215\t   two-stage reduction patterns before implementing c001; record usage.\n216\t2. Implement `solution/solution.py` for the current `cNNN` (Triton kernel +\n217\t   thin PyTorch wrapper: alloc, pre-zero accumulators, launch, return tuple).\n218\t3. Run pre-eval correctness checks (§3.1–3.4).\n219\t4. Evaluate: `./scripts/evaluate_candidate.sh feedback cNNN`.\n220\t5. Append the §6 record to `candidates.jsonl`.\n221\t6. Decide keep/iterate/revert; advance the ladder (§2) by one change.\n222\t7. Re-check budget & stopping criteria (§5) after every eval.\n223\t8. On convergence, write `SEARCH_COMPLETE`; never `final` without approval.\n224\t\n225\t---\n226\t\n227\t## 8. Decision log (append-only)\n228\t\n229\t### c001 — evaluated, FAIL (revert)\n230\t- **Result:** 0/5 pass — **uniform `RUNTIME_ERROR`** on every workload, including\n231\t  the smallest (f2508211, 1024 rows). No `sol_ms`/`max_abs` recorded ⇒ the kernel\n232\t  never produced output (compile/launch-time failure, not a numeric mismatch and\n233\t  not shape-specific).\n234\t- **Diagnosis:** Design A held `BLOCK_H = next_pow2(2304) = 4096` with\n235\t  `num_warps=8` (256 threads) and ~25+ live fp32 length-4096 vectors\n236\t  (h0..2, gc0..2, act, nw, rw0..2, plus nrm/scl/innov/pred/ga/gpred/ghs/… ).\n237\t  At 4096/256 = 16 elems/lane × ~25 arrays ≈ 400 registers/thread this blows the\n238\t  per-block register budget → \"too many resources requested for launch\". The\n239\t  math was cross-checked analytically against the reference and is believed\n240\t  correct; this is purely a **resource/occupancy** failure.\n241\t- **Decision:** revert Design-A-as-is. The math derivation stands and is reused.\n242\t- **Pivot for next candidate (register-pressure reduction — new `cNNN`):**\n243\t  bring the kernel within the launch budget by (a) raising `num_warps`\n244\t  (16/32) so per-lane element count drops, and/or (b) shrinking the working set:\n245\t  stream `router_weight[3,H]` from L2 instead of holding `rw0/rw1/rw2` resident,\n246\t  recompute cheap vectors (`scl` from `nrm`) instead of storing, and reuse buffers\n247\t  aggressively. This effectively promotes the planned c002 (occupancy tuning) into\n248\t  a *correctness-enabling* rung and merges the c003 register-relief ideas forward,\n249\t  since without a launching kernel there is no baseline to tune against.\n250\t  Keep exactly one meaningful change set per new immutable candidate ID and\n251\t  re-evaluate once. Correctness canaries (f2508211 atol 0.0029, a6c812e5 0.0045)\n252\t  and the large-row perf canary (fcd64c92) remain as before.\n253\t\n254\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9806933-2899-41b5-90ed-01d25aa07f47","uuid":"c791c082-0735-4f60-845c-df4b06b23fb5","timestamp":"2026-09-17T19:42:04.836Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-040_altup_predict_correction_cycle_backward/docs/plan.md","content":"  \"reason\": \"<one line>\",\n  \"cumulative_evals\": 1,\n  \"skills_used\": [\"KernelWiki?\"],\n  \"tokens_note\": \"optional budget snapshot\"\n}\n```\nRules: `decision` ∈ {keep, revert, iterate}; `parent` links lineage (c002.parent\n= c001, etc.); fill actual speedups/margins from evaluator output; keep records\nimmutable once written.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Execution checklist (workflow guardrails)\n\n1. Consult **KernelWiki** for A800/`sm_80` RMSNorm-backward fusion + atomic /\n   two-stage reduction patterns before implementing c001; record usage.\n2. Implement `solution/solution.py` for the current `cNNN` (Triton kernel +\n   thin PyTorch wrapper: alloc, pre-zero accumulators, launch, return tuple).\n3. Run pre-eval correctness checks (§3.1–3.4).\n4. Evaluate: `./scripts/evaluate_candidate.sh feedback cNNN`.\n5. Append the §6 record to `candidates.jsonl`.\n6. Decide keep/iterate/revert; advance the ladder (§2) by one change.\n7. Re-check budget & stopping criteria (§5) after every eval.\n8. On convergence, write `SEARCH_COMPLETE`; never `final` without approval.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Decision log (append-only)\n\n### c001 — evaluated, FAIL (revert)\n- **Result:** 0/5 pass — **uniform `RUNTIME_ERROR`** on every workload, including\n  the smallest (f2508211, 1024 rows). No `sol_ms`/`max_abs` recorded ⇒ the kernel\n  never produced output (compile/launch-time failure, not a numeric mismatch and\n  not shape-specific).\n- **Diagnosis:** Design A held `BLOCK_H = next_pow2(2304) = 4096` with\n  `num_warps=8` (256 threads) and ~25+ live fp32 length-4096 vectors\n  (h0..2, gc0..2, act, nw, rw0..2, plus nrm/scl/innov/pred/ga/gpred/ghs/… ).\n  At 4096/256 = 16 elems/lane × ~25 arrays ≈ 400 registers/thread this blows the\n  per-block register budget → \"too many resources requested for launch\". The\n  math was cross-checked analytically against the reference and is believed\n  correct; this is purely a **resource/occupancy** failure.\n- **Decision:** revert Design-A-as-is. The math derivation stands and is reused.\n- **Pivot for next candidate (register-pressure reduction — new `cNNN`):**\n  bring the kernel within the launch budget by (a) raising `num_warps`\n  (16/32) so per-lane element count drops, and/or (b) shrinking the working set:\n  stream `router_weight[3,H]` from L2 instead of holding `rw0/rw1/rw2` resident,\n  recompute cheap vectors (`scl` from `nrm`) instead of storing, and reuse buffers\n  aggressively. This effectively promotes the planned c002 (occupancy tuning) into\n  a *correctness-enabling* rung and merges the c003 register-relief ideas forward,\n  since without a launching kernel there is no baseline to tune against.\n  Keep exactly one meaningful change set per new immutable candidate ID and\n  re-evaluate once. Correctness canaries (f2508211 atol 0.0029, a6c812e5 0.0045)\n  and the large-row perf canary (fcd64c92) remain as before.\n\n","numLines":55,"startLine":200,"totalLines":254}}}
