\"candidate\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c004\", \"source_hash\": \"3ae122ae1e35627dcf1ece208802a8bd719f50e3b34b18764ef785e51ce611c1\", \"design\": \"DIAGNOSTIC candidate: kernel body byte-identical to c004; only run() changed to wrap the launch in try/except that appends traceback.format_exc() to docs/diag_c005.txt (inside the task workspace) and RE-RAISES the original exception. No fallback, no result fabrication, exception not swallowed -> candidate still legitimately fails.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Persisting the traceback will reveal the true compile/runtime cause hidden behind the evaluator's opaque RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"change_from_parent\": \"added try/except+traceback-to-file+re-raise around the launch; no math/config change\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"kernel math unchanged from c004\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"SUCCESS as a diagnostic: docs/diag_c005.txt captured the true cause for all 5 shapes -> triton.compiler.errors.CompilationError NotImplementedError('only tuple comprehensions are supported') at the line `pcw = [[tl.load(...) for q in range(3)] for p in range(9)]`. This Triton build (evaluator venv, py3.12) does NOT support Python LIST comprehensions inside @triton.jit; only TUPLE comprehensions. Every candidate c001-c005 used list comprehensions / list literals of triton values, so all failed identically at compile. Fix for c006: rewrite the kernel with ZERO list comprehensions and no list literals holding triton values -- fully unroll N=3 with explicit named scalars (and use tuple(...) or explicit loops where iteration is needed). Also revert the diagnostic try/except so run() is clean. Interpreter path confirms python3.12 build.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 5, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 5 of 100 budget; diagnostic paid off - root cause is list-comprehension unsupported\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c006\", \"parent\": \"c005\", \"source_hash\": \"21b2877898e0a8524fec9ad79c76c8db84176faf7334b5249d621e9eb1b0e350\", \"design\": \"Fully-unrolled 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Removed ALL list comprehensions and list literals of triton values (the c001-c005 compile blocker): pcw/ccw loaded into 27+9 named scalars; mod/flat/C/acoef/g_flat/ghs all explicit named scalars; IDX-dependent branches via if IDX==... on constexpr. Clean run() (diagnostic try/except removed). exp-based _tanh. PassA variance+router dots; PassB g_acoef & g_flat; PassC mbar + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD stores grad_activated & grad_hidden.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Removing list comprehensions (root cause found in c005) yields a compiling, correct fused kernel that beats the multi-kernel reference (H1 fusion)\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite to eliminate list comprehensions/list literals; revert diagnostic instrumentation\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to verified derivation; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred[idx]-=g_innov before g_flat & ghs use); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum predict+correct; accumulators pre-zeroed; fp32 math cast only at store; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes match spec; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.268013674035502, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 20.6345815, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.363762324057112, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.34516, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.351436603181414, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.6643275, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.276650719493298, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 8.6875375, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.316672500584138, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.6755465, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.315135988894236, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"FIRST WORKING CANDIDATE. 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.3151x. Confirms the list-comprehension root cause and the H1 fusion hypothesis. max_abs 0.03125 within per-workload atol margins at match_ratio 0.98/0.99; max_rel ~0.0078 << 0.05. New baseline/best. Next: perf tuning (Design B row-blocking to cut atomic contention on grad_rw/grad_nw; BLOCK/num_warps sweep), one change per candidate.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 6, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 6 of 100 budget; first valid candidate, geomean 4.3151x\"}\n\n\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":6,"newStart":4,"newLines":7,"lines":[" {\"candidate\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_hash\": \"2d4c270f23c17a5da81cd35ba225ff51dbfc7636fef07ca3f8f117e5297af1c0\", \"design\": \"Same 4-pass H-tiled kernel as c003 (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Only change: replaced tl.sigmoid-based tanh with a device helper _tanh built from tl.abs/tl.exp/tl.where (overflow-safe: t=(1-e^{-2|x|})/(1+e^{-2|x|}); sign via where).\", \"hypothesis\": \"H(intrinsic): tl.sigmoid was the shared compile-time failure; an exp-based tanh removes the dependency and lets the kernel launch\", \"change_from_parent\": \"tanh implementation: 2*sigmoid(2x)-1 -> exp/abs/where helper (no tl.sigmoid)\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"identical math to c003; _tanh numerically equals tanh; all gradient formulas unchanged and re-verified vs reference\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged from c003\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"Intrinsic hypothesis DISPROVEN: still uniform RUNTIME_ERROR with exp-based tanh, and inspection of the installed Triton (.venv/.../triton/language/__init__.py exports 'sigmoid') shows tl.sigmoid is in fact available -- so sigmoid was never the issue. Four candidates now fail identically with no traceback exposed by the evaluator (feedback.json/log carry only status=RUNTIME_ERROR, sol_ms=null => run() raises during first invocation). Since I cannot execute Triton/CUDA/python here to read the error, the next candidate c005 will INSTRUMENT run(): wrap the kernel launch in try/except that writes the full traceback to a file inside the task workspace (docs/diag_c005.txt) and then RE-RAISES (candidate still legitimately fails, no computational fallback). This surfaces the actual compile/runtime error text for precise fixing.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 4, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 4 of 100 budget\"}"," {\"candidate\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c004\", \"source_hash\": \"3ae122ae1e35627dcf1ece208802a8bd719f50e3b34b18764ef785e51ce611c1\", \"design\": \"DIAGNOSTIC candidate: kernel body byte-identical to c004; only run() changed to wrap the launch in try/except that appends traceback.format_exc() to docs/diag_c005.txt (inside the task workspace) and RE-RAISES the original exception. No fallback, no result fabrication, exception not swallowed -> candidate still legitimately fails.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Persisting the traceback will reveal the true compile/runtime cause hidden behind the evaluator's opaque RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"change_from_parent\": \"added try/except+traceback-to-file+re-raise around the launch; no math/config change\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"kernel math unchanged from c004\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"SUCCESS as a diagnostic: docs/diag_c005.txt captured the true cause for all 5 shapes -> triton.compiler.errors.CompilationError NotImplementedError('only tuple comprehensions are supported') at the line `pcw = [[tl.load(...) for q in range(3)] for p in range(9)]`. This Triton build (evaluator venv, py3.12) does NOT support Python LIST comprehensions inside @triton.jit; only TUPLE comprehensions. Every candidate c001-c005 used list comprehensions / list literals of triton values, so all failed identically at compile. Fix for c006: rewrite the kernel with ZERO list comprehensions and no list literals holding triton values -- fully unroll N=3 with explicit named scalars (and use tuple(...) or explicit loops where iteration is needed). Also revert the diagnostic try/except so run() is clean. Interpreter path confirms python3.12 build.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 5, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 5 of 100 budget; diagnostic paid off - root cause is list-comprehension unsupported\"}"," {\"candidate\": \"c006\", \"parent\": \"c005\", \"source_hash\": \"21b2877898e0a8524fec9ad79c76c8db84176faf7334b5249d621e9eb1b0e350\", \"design\": \"Fully-unrolled 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Removed ALL list comprehensions and list literals of triton values (the c001-c005 compile blocker): pcw/ccw loaded into 27+9 named scalars; mod/flat/C/acoef/g_flat/ghs all explicit named scalars; IDX-dependent branches via if IDX==... on constexpr. Clean run() (diagnostic try/except removed). exp-based _tanh. PassA variance+router dots; PassB g_acoef & g_flat; PassC mbar + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD stores grad_activated & grad_hidden.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Removing list comprehensions (root cause found in c005) yields a compiling, correct fused kernel that beats the multi-kernel reference (H1 fusion)\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite to eliminate list comprehensions/list literals; revert diagnostic instrumentation\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to verified derivation; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred[idx]-=g_innov before g_flat & ghs use); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum predict+correct; accumulators pre-zeroed; fp32 math cast only at store; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes match spec; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.268013674035502, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 20.6345815, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.363762324057112, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.34516, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.351436603181414, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.6643275, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.276650719493298, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 8.6875375, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.316672500584138, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.6755465, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.315135988894236, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"FIRST WORKING CANDIDATE. 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.3151x. Confirms the list-comprehension root cause and the H1 fusion hypothesis. max_abs 0.03125 within per-workload atol margins at match_ratio 0.98/0.99; max_rel ~0.0078 << 0.05. New baseline/best. Next: perf tuning (Design B row-blocking to cut atomic contention on grad_rw/grad_nw; BLOCK/num_warps sweep), one change per candidate.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 6, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 6 of 100 budget; first valid candidate, geomean 4.3151x\"}","+{\"candidate\": \"c007\", \"parent\": \"c006\", \"source_hash\": \"587df6bf53af282adfcc117eabb8145fdd76a252430e58d7f7286dfb55566fca\", \"design\": \"Single-pass, fully H-resident rewrite: grid=rows, BLOCK_H=next_pow2(H)=4096 masked, num_warps=16. Each heavy vector (h0/h1/h2, gc0/1/2, activated, norm_weight, rw0/1/2) loaded EXACTLY ONCE; all H-reductions (var_p/var_c, router dots, g_acoef, g_flat, mbar_c/mbar_p) computed on the resident vectors; then grad_rw/grad_nw atomics and stores in the same program. No list comprehensions (all named scalars). Contrasts c006 which re-read tensors across 4 tiled passes. num_warps=16 keeps per-thread reg count under the c001 overflow point at BLOCK_H=4096.\", \"hypothesis\": \"H(single-pass): eliminating the 3-4x redundant HBM re-reads of c006 cuts memory traffic toward the ~11*H floor and improves geomean, provided the resident working set still launches\", \"change_from_parent\": \"4-pass tiled BLOCK=256/num_warps=4 -> single-pass BLOCK_H=4096 resident/num_warps=16; math identical\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to c006 (verified); idx-subtraction ordering preserved; g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum both steps; accumulators pre-zeroed; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H; return order/dtypes match; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.574453637524444, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 19.252283, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.6488310955969565, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.0787125, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.681700213858796, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.6174635, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.556946711711721, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 8.1531705, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.589020792693895, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.5761065, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.609948936385272, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"IMPROVED over c006: 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.6099x vs 4.3151x (+6.8%). Single-pass read-once confirms the redundant-re-read hypothesis. Same numerics (max_abs 0.03125, max_rel ~0.0078). New best. Note: BLOCK_H=4096 masked wastes ~44% lanes (H=2304); next c008 tries num_warps sweep (8) and/or exact register tuning; a later candidate can try Design B row-blocking to cut grad_rw/grad_nw atomic contention on the 39232-row workload.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 7, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 7 of 100 budget; new best geomean 4.6099x\"}"," "," "," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f3a47736-844a-4d50-9946-e0271ff1121d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0163JPyjYP51jds8JUyhvXSQ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-040_altup_predict_correction_cycle_backward/docs/plan.md","old_string":"- Keep c006 as the fallback best; only promote a candidate that beats 4.3151×.","new_string":"- Keep c006 as the fallback best; only promote a candidate that beats 4.3151×.\n\n### c007 — evaluated, PASS (keep) — NEW BEST 4.6099×\n- **Change:** single-pass, fully H-resident rewrite — grid=rows, `BLOCK_H=4096`\n  masked, `num_warps=16`. Every heavy vector loaded once; all H-reductions on the\n  resident vectors; atomics + stores in the same program. Math identical to c006.\n- **Result:** 5/5 PASSED, **geomean 4.6099×** (was 4.3151×, **+6.8%**). Same\n  numerics (`max_abs=0.03125`, `max_rel≈0.0078`).\n- **Decision:** keep — new best. Confirms the redundant-re-read hypothesis: c006\n  re-read the heavy tensors across 4 tiled passes; c007 reads once.\n- **Note:** `BLOCK_H=4096` masked wastes ~44% lanes for `H=2304`. `num_warps=16`\n  was needed to fit the resident working set (c001's `num_warps=8`+4096 overflowed\n  registers).\n\n### Next steps (from c007 best)\n- **c008 — `num_warps` sweep** on the single-pass kernel (try 8; maybe 32). Pure\n  launch-config change, tests occupancy vs the 44% lane waste.\n- **cN — Design B row-blocking:** amortize `grad_rw`/`grad_nw` atomics across\n  rows (biggest expected win on the 39232-row workload fcd64c92, currently the\n  lowest per-workload speedup at 4.57×).\n- **cN — two-stage reduction** if atomics still dominate.\n- Only promote a candidate that beats 4.6099×; else keep c007.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":183332,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,