's opaque RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"change_from_parent\": \"added try/except+traceback-to-file+re-raise around the launch; no math/config change\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"kernel math unchanged from c004\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"SUCCESS as a diagnostic: docs/diag_c005.txt captured the true cause for all 5 shapes -> triton.compiler.errors.CompilationError NotImplementedError('only tuple comprehensions are supported') at the line `pcw = [[tl.load(...) for q in range(3)] for p in range(9)]`. This Triton build (evaluator venv, py3.12) does NOT support Python LIST comprehensions inside @triton.jit; only TUPLE comprehensions. Every candidate c001-c005 used list comprehensions / list literals of triton values, so all failed identically at compile. Fix for c006: rewrite the kernel with ZERO list comprehensions and no list literals holding triton values -- fully unroll N=3 with explicit named scalars (and use tuple(...) or explicit loops where iteration is needed). Also revert the diagnostic try/except so run() is clean. Interpreter path confirms python3.12 build.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 5, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 5 of 100 budget; diagnostic paid off - root cause is list-comprehension unsupported\"}"," {\"candidate\": \"c006\", \"parent\": \"c005\", \"source_hash\": \"21b2877898e0a8524fec9ad79c76c8db84176faf7334b5249d621e9eb1b0e350\", \"design\": \"Fully-unrolled 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Removed ALL list comprehensions and list literals of triton values (the c001-c005 compile blocker): pcw/ccw loaded into 27+9 named scalars; mod/flat/C/acoef/g_flat/ghs all explicit named scalars; IDX-dependent branches via if IDX==... on constexpr. Clean run() (diagnostic try/except removed). exp-based _tanh. PassA variance+router dots; PassB g_acoef & g_flat; PassC mbar + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD stores grad_activated & grad_hidden.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Removing list comprehensions (root cause found in c005) yields a compiling, correct fused kernel that beats the multi-kernel reference (H1 fusion)\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite to eliminate list comprehensions/list literals; revert diagnostic instrumentation\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to verified derivation; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred[idx]-=g_innov before g_flat & ghs use); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum predict+correct; accumulators pre-zeroed; fp32 math cast only at store; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes match spec; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.268013674035502, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 20.6345815, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.363762324057112, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.34516, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007812