c_checks\": \"term-by-term vs reference OK; idx-subtraction ordering (gpred[idx]-=g_innov before predict-backward) applied; g_flat[3*a+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a] index order applied; router/norm grads sum both steps; four accumulated outputs pre-zeroed; fp32 math cast only at store; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"grid=rows; variant k base (k*rows+row)*H; activated base row*H; return tuple order/dtypes match spec\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"Uniform RUNTIME_ERROR across all 5 shapes (incl. smallest 1024 rows) => compile/resource-time failure, not shape-specific. Most likely cause: BLOCK_H=4096 with num_warps=8 holds ~25+ live fp32 vectors (~400 regs/thread) exceeding the register budget. Next candidate: cut register pressure (num_warps=16/32 and/or fewer live arrays / recompute) to get a compiling kernel; math verified correct analytically.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 1, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 1 of 100 budget\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_hash\": \"f73a7225c123a11cb5886e1ed5090efa6abd0aed5b617c25090e54931bc6f9ff\", \"design\": \"Same fused Design A kernel body as c001 (BLOCK_H=4096 masked, fully H-resident, ~11 input + ~20 derived length-4096 fp32 arrays live end-to-end), only launch change: num_warps 8 -> 32\", \"hypothesis\": \"H2 occupancy: raising num_warps lowers per-lane element count enough to fit the register budget and let the kernel launch\", \"change_from_parent\": \"num_warps 8 -> 32 (no math change)\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"identical math to c001 (verified); pure launch-config change\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged from c001\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"Still uniform RUNTIME_ERROR at num_warps=32 => not fixable by occupancy tuning. Root cause refined: BLOCK_H=4096 keeps the whole working set resident; the persistent live set of ~30 length-4096 fp32 arrays exceeds the per-thread 255-register cap regardless of warp count (more warps cannot reduce per-thread live values here since each lane still owns 4096/threads elements x many arrays). Correct fix is to TILE the H axis (multi-pass over small BLOCK chunks) so only a handful of small arrays are live per pass, recomputing per-tile quantities. Next candidate c003: 4-pass tiled kernel, BLOCK=768, num_warps=4.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 2, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 2 of 100 budget\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c003\", \"parent\": \"c002\", \"source_hash\": \"d05db2142aa8d5514adffbde4ee20a95ecb6a0ab9f2cafc0f7ae5d06e19e7a7e\", \"design\": \"Rewritten as a 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, exact 9*256=2304, num_warps=4). PassA: variance+router dots; PassB: g_acoef & g_flat reductions; PassC: mbar reductions + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD: stores grad_activated & grad_hidden. Only 3-vec/9-vec scalar state persists across passes; per-tile arrays are length-256 -> tiny register footprint. Still uses tl.sigmoid for tanh.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Tiling H to a small BLOCK eliminates the register-file overflow and lets the kernel launch/compile\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite: monolithic BLOCK_H=4096 -> 4-pass tiled BLOCK=256; num_warps 32 -> 4\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math re-derived identically to reference; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred=gc-[a==IDX]*g_innov before g_flat & ghs); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; router/norm grads sum both steps; accumulators pre-zeroed; recompute of scl/nrm per tile is exact\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"CRITICAL FINDING: the tiny tiled kernel (only length-256 arrays live per pass, num_warps=4) STILL fails identically -> register pressure was NOT the cause. The real common cause is a structural/API issue shared by c001,c002,c003. The one version-sensitive intrinsic present in ALL three is tl.sigmoid (used to build tanh). If tl.sigmoid is unavailable/rejected in this Triton build, every candidate errors at compile regardless of tiling. Next candidate c004: replace tl.sigmoid(2x) with exp-based sigmoid 1/(1+exp(-2x)) using tl.exp (universally available); keep the tiled structure.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 3, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 3 of 100 budget\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_hash\": \"2d4c270f23c17a5da81cd35ba225ff51dbfc7636fef07ca3f8f117e5297af1c0\", \"design\": \"Same 4-pass H-tiled kernel as c003 (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Only change: replaced tl.sigmoid-based tanh with a device helper _tanh built from tl.abs/tl.exp/tl.where (overflow-safe: t=(1-e^{-2|x|})/(1+e^{-2|x|}); sign via where).\", \"hypothesis\": \"H(intrinsic): tl.sigmoid was the shared compile-time failure; an exp-based tanh removes the dependency and lets the kernel launch\", \"change_from_parent\": \"tanh implementation: 2*sigmoid(2x)-1 -> exp/abs/where helper (no tl.sigmoid)\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"identical math to c003; _tanh numerically equals tanh; all gradient formulas unchanged and re-verified vs reference\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged from c003\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"Intrinsic hypothesis DISPROVEN: still uniform RUNTIME_ERROR with exp-based tanh, and inspection of the installed Triton (.venv/.../triton/language/__init__.py exports 'sigmoid') shows tl.sigmoid is in fact available -- so sigmoid was never the issue. Four candidates now fail identically with no traceback exposed by the evaluator (feedback.json/log carry only status=RUNTIME_ERROR, sol_ms=null => run() raises during first invocation). Since I cannot execute Triton/CUDA/python here to read the error, the next candidate c005 will INSTRUMENT run(): wrap the kernel launch in try/except that writes the full traceback to a file inside the task workspace (docs/diag_c005.txt) and then RE-RAISES (candidate still legitimately fails, no computational fallback). This surfaces the actual compile/runtime error text for precise fixing.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 4, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 4 of 100 budget\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c004\", \"source_hash\": \"3ae122ae1e35627dcf1ece208802a8bd719f50e3b34b18764ef785e51ce611c1\", \"design\": \"DIAGNOSTIC candidate: kernel body byte-identical to c004; only run() changed to wrap the launch in try/except that appends traceback.format_exc() to docs/diag_c005.txt (inside the task workspace) and RE-RAISES the original exception. No fallback, no result fabrication, exception not swallowed -> candidate still legitimately fails.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Persisting the traceback will reveal the true compile/runtime cause hidden behind the evaluator's opaque RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"change_from_parent\": \"added try/except+traceback-to-file+re-raise around the launch; no math/config change\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"kernel math unchanged from c004\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"SUCCESS as a diagnostic: docs/diag_c005.txt captured the true cause for all 5 shapes -> triton.compiler.errors.CompilationError NotImplementedError('only tuple comprehensions are supported') at the line `pcw = [[tl.load(...) for q in range(3)] for p in range(9)]`. This Triton build (evaluator venv, py3.12) does NOT support Python LIST comprehensions inside @triton.jit; only TUPLE comprehensions. Every candidate c001-c005 used list comprehensions / list literals of triton values, so all failed identically at compile. Fix for c006: rewrite the kernel with ZERO list comprehensions and no list literals holding triton values -- fully unroll N=3 with explicit named scalars (and use tuple(...) or explicit loops where iteration is needed). Also revert the diagnostic try/except so run() is clean. Interpreter path confirms python3.12 build.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 5, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 5 of 100 budget; diagnostic paid off - root cause is list-comprehension unsupported\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c006\", \"parent\": \"c005\", \"source_hash\": \"21b2877898e0a8524fec9ad79c76c8db84176faf7334b5249d621e9eb1b0e350\", \"design\": \"Fully-unrolled 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Removed ALL list comprehensions and list literals of triton values (the c001-c005 compile blocker): pcw/ccw loaded into 27+9 named scalars; mod/flat/C/acoef/g_flat/ghs all explicit named scalars; IDX-dependent branches via if IDX==... on constexpr. Clean run() (diagnostic try/except removed). exp-based _tanh. PassA variance+router dots; PassB g_acoef & g_flat; PassC mbar + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD stores grad_activated & grad_hidden.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Removing list comprehensions (root cause found in c005) yields a compiling, correct fused kernel that beats the multi-kernel reference (H1 fusion)\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite to eliminate list comprehensions/list literals; revert diagnostic instrumentation\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to verified derivation; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred[idx]-=g_innov before g_flat & ghs use); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum predict+correct; accumulators pre-zeroed; fp32 math cast only at store; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes match spec; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.268013674035502, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 20.6345815, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.363762324057112, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.34516, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.351436603181414, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.6643275, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.276650719493298, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 8.6875375, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.316672500584138, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.6755465, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.315135988894236, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"FIRST WORKING CANDIDATE. 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.3151x. Confirms the list-comprehension root cause and the H1 fusion hypothesis. max_abs 0.03125 within per-workload atol margins at match_ratio 0.98/0.99; max_rel ~0.0078 << 0.05. New baseline/best. Next: perf tuning (Design B row-blocking to cut atomic contention on grad_rw/grad_nw; BLOCK/num_warps sweep), one change per candidate.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 6, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 6 of 100 budget; first valid candidate, geomean 4.3151x\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c007\", \"parent\": \"c006\", \"source_hash\": \"587df6bf53af282adfcc117eabb8145fdd76a252430e58d7f7286dfb55566fca\", \"design\": \"Single-pass, fully H-resident rewrite: grid=rows, BLOCK_H=next_pow2(H)=4096 masked, num_warps=16. Each heavy vector (h0/h1/h2, gc0/1/2, activated, norm_weight, rw0/1/2) loaded EXACTLY ONCE; all H-reductions (var_p/var_c, router dots, g_acoef, g_flat, mbar_c/mbar_p) computed on the resident vectors; then grad_rw/grad_nw atomics and stores in the same program. No list comprehensions (all named scalars). Contrasts c006 which re-read tensors across 4 tiled passes. num_warps=16 keeps per-thread reg count under the c001 overflow point at BLOCK_H=4096.\", \"hypothesis\": \"H(single-pass): eliminating the 3-4x redundant HBM re-reads of c006 cuts memory traffic toward the ~11*H floor and improves geomean, provided the resident working set still launches\", \"change_from_parent\": \"4-pass tiled BLOCK=256/num_warps=4 -> single-pass BLOCK_H=4096 resident/num_warps=16; math identical\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to c006 (verified); idx-subtraction ordering preserved; g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum both steps; accumulators pre-zeroed; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H; return order/dtypes match; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.574453637524444, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 19.252283, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.6488310955969565, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.0787125, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.681700213858796, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.6174635, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.556946711711721, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 8.1531705, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.589020792693895, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.5761065, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.609948936385272, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"IMPROVED over c006: 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.6099x vs 4.3151x (+6.8%). Single-pass read-once confirms the redundant-re-read hypothesis. Same numerics (max_abs 0.03125, max_rel ~0.0078). New best. Note: BLOCK_H=4096 masked wastes ~44% lanes (H=2304); next c008 tries num_warps sweep (8) and/or exact register tuning; a later candidate can try Design B row-blocking to cut grad_rw/grad_nw atomic contention on the 39232-row workload.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 7, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 7 of 100 budget; new best geomean 4.6099x\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c008\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_hash\": \"f9b28ae987e6c072e875ceb03ddb96a22cab0ffdbb419780332e72015ec6be6c\", \"design\": \"Design B row-blocking: grid=cdiv(rows,BLOCK_ROWS) with BLOCK_ROWS=8, BLOCK_H=4096 masked, num_warps=16. Each program owns 8 consecutive rows; router_weight/norm_weight and the 27+9 coef scalars loaded ONCE per program; grad_router[3,H], grad_norm[H], grad_pcw[9,3], grad_ccw[3,3] accumulated in local fp32 registers/SRAM across the 8 rows and flushed with a SINGLE atomic set per program (~8x fewer atomics). Per-row math is the c007 single-pass H-resident body. row<rows guard via lmask. No list comprehensions.\", \"hypothesis\": \"H4 atomics: amortizing grad_rw/grad_nw atomics across 8 rows + loading shared weights once cuts atomic contention (esp. on the 39232-row workload) and improves geomean\", \"change_from_parent\": \"single-row single-pass -> 8-row-blocked program with local accumulation + single atomic flush; grid shrinks 8x\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"per-row math identical to c007 (verified); local accumulators sum correctly across rows (grad_rw/grad_nw/gpcw/gccw are pure sums over rows); lmask=m&(row<rows) prevents OOB and contributes 0 to accumulators for tail rows; idx-subtraction ordering and g_flat index order preserved\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H; single flush writes match [3,H]/[H]/[9,3]/[3,3]; return order/dtypes match; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 8.615327335024078, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 10.222325, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 8.276720023850752, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 2.290913, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 5.685931995696379, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.508409, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 8.517697860726875, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 4.3619255, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 7.110471174850227, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.017202, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 7.551451960435094, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"BIG WIN: 5/5 PASSED, geomean 7.5515x vs c007 4.6099x (+64%). Confirms H4 atomics hypothesis - atomic contention on grad_rw/grad_nw was a major cost. Large-row workloads jump most (fcd64c92 4.57->8.62x, e9c4303d 4.56->8.52x); small-B f2508211 gains least (4.68->5.69x, fewer rows per program to amortize + tail waste). New best. Next: sweep BLOCK_ROWS (16/32) and num_warps to push further; small-B workloads may prefer smaller BLOCK_ROWS but one immutable config must serve all 5.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 8, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 8 of 100 budget; new best geomean 7.5515x\"}\n\n\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":6,"newStart":6,"newLines":7,"lines":[" {\"candidate\": \"c