input + ~20 derived length-4096 fp32 arrays live end-to-end), only launch change: num_warps 8 -> 32\", \"hypothesis\": \"H2 occupancy: raising num_warps lowers per-lane element count enough to fit the register budget and let the kernel launch\", \"change_from_parent\": \"num_warps 8 -> 32 (no math change)\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"identical math to c001 (verified); pure launch-config change\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged from c001\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"Still uniform RUNTIME_ERROR at num_warps=32 => not fixable by occupancy tuning. Root cause refined: BLOCK_H=4096 keeps the whole working set resident; the persistent live set of ~30 length-4096 fp32 arrays exceeds the per-thread 255-register cap regardless of warp count (more warps cannot reduce per-thread live values here since each lane still owns 4096/threads elements x many arrays). Correct fix is to TILE the H axis (multi-pass over small BLOCK chunks) so only a handful of small arrays are live per pass, recomputing per-tile quantities. Next candidate c003: 4-pass tiled kernel, BLOCK=768, num_warps=4.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 2, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 2 of 100 budget\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c003\", \"parent\": \"c002\", \"source_hash\": \"d05db2142aa8d5514adffbde4ee20a95ecb6a0ab9f2cafc0f7ae5d06e19e7a7e\", \"design\": \"Rewritten as a 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, exact 9*256=2304, num_warps=4). PassA: variance+router dots; PassB: g_acoef & g_flat reductions; PassC: mbar reductions + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD: stores grad_activated & grad_hidden. Only 3-vec/9-vec scalar state persists across passes; per-tile arrays are length-256 -> tiny register footprint. Still uses tl.sigmoid for tanh.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Tiling H to a small BLOCK eliminates the register-file overflow and lets the kernel launch/compile\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite: monolithic BLOCK_H=4096 -> 4-pass tiled BLOCK=256; num_warps 32 -> 4\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math re-derived identically to reference; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred=gc-[a==IDX]*g_innov before g_flat & ghs); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; router/norm grads sum both steps; accumulators pre-zeroed; recompute of scl/nrm per tile is exact\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"CRITICAL FINDING: the tiny tiled kernel (only length-256 arrays live per pass, num_warps=4) STILL fails identically -> register pressure was NOT the cause. The real common cause is a structural/API issue shared by c001,c002,c003. The one version-sensitive intrinsic present in ALL three is tl.sigmoid (used to build tanh). If tl.sigmoid is unavailable/rejected in this Triton build, every candidate errors at compile regardless of tiling. Next candidate c004: replace tl.sigmoid(2x) with exp-based sigmoid 1/(1+exp(-2x)) using tl.exp (universally available); keep the tiled structure.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 3, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 3 of 100 budget\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c004\", \"parent\": \"c003\", \"source_hash\": \"2d4c270f23c17a5da81cd35ba225ff51dbfc7636fef07ca3f8f117e5297af1c0\", \"design\": \"Same 4-pass H-tiled kernel as c003 (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Only change: replaced tl.sigmoid-based tanh with a device helper _tanh built from tl.abs/tl.exp/tl.where (overflow-safe: t=(1-e^{-2|x|})/(1+e^{-2|x|}); sign via where).\", \"hypothesis\": \"H(intrinsic): tl.sigmoid was the shared compile-time failure; an exp-based tanh removes the dependency and lets the kernel launch\", \"change_from_parent\": \"tanh implementation: 2*sigmoid(2x)-1 -> exp/abs/where helper (no tl.sigmoid)\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"identical math to c003; _tanh numerically equals tanh; all gradient formulas unchanged and re-verified vs reference\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged from c003\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"u