e launch; no math/config change\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"kernel math unchanged from c004\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"pass\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"all_pass\": false, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"SUCCESS as a diagnostic: docs/diag_c005.txt captured the true cause for all 5 shapes -> triton.compiler.errors.CompilationError NotImplementedError('only tuple comprehensions are supported') at the line `pcw = [[tl.load(...) for q in range(3)] for p in range(9)]`. This Triton build (evaluator venv, py3.12) does NOT support Python LIST comprehensions inside @triton.jit; only TUPLE comprehensions. Every candidate c001-c005 used list comprehensions / list literals of triton values, so all failed identically at compile. Fix for c006: rewrite the kernel with ZERO list comprehensions and no list literals holding triton values -- fully unroll N=3 with explicit named scalars (and use tuple(...) or explicit loops where iteration is needed). Also revert the diagnostic try/except so run() is clean. Interpreter path confirms python3.12 build.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 5, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 5 of 100 budget; diagnostic paid off - root cause is list-comprehension unsupported\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c006\", \"parent\": \"c005\", \"source_hash\": \"21b2877898e0a8524fec9ad79c76c8db84176faf7334b5249d621e9eb1b0e350\", \"design\": \"Fully-unrolled 4-pass H-tiled kernel (BLOCK=256, NUM_TILES=9, num_warps=4). Removed ALL list comprehensions and list literals of triton values (the c001-c005 compile blocker): pcw/ccw loaded into 27+9 named scalars; mod/flat/C/acoef/g_flat/ghs all explicit named scalars; IDX-dependent branches via if IDX==... on constexpr. Clean run() (diagnostic try/except removed). exp-based _tanh. PassA variance+router dots; PassB g_acoef & g_flat; PassC mbar + grad_rw/grad_nw atomics; PassD stores grad_activated & grad_hidden.\", \"hypothesis\": \"Removing list comprehensions (root cause found in c005) yields a compiling, correct fused kernel that beats the multi-kernel reference (H1 fusion)\", \"change_from_parent\": \"full rewrite to eliminate list comprehensions/list literals; revert diagnostic instrumentation\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"math identical to verified derivation; idx-subtraction ordering preserved (gpred[idx]-=g_innov before g_flat & ghs use); g_flat[a*3+c]=sum_h hidden[c]*gpred[a]; C[m][n]=flat[n*3+m]; router/norm grads sum predict+correct; accumulators pre-zeroed; fp32 math cast only at store; exact 1/2304\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k*rows+row)*H, activated row*H; return order/dtypes match spec; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.268013674035502, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 20.6345815, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"5834489e-1f51-5995-b499-8765bd31a705\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 128, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.363762324057112, \"ref_ms\": 18.9612455, \"sol_ms\": 4.34516, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"f2508211-757f-5c74-a08a-621ce070f77d\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.351436603181414, \"ref_ms\": 2.890779, \"sol_ms\": 0.6643275, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.007751937955617905}, {\"uuid\": \"e9c4303d-4391-5cb3-a6e1-674c1d19bbfd\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 256, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.276650719493298, \"ref_ms\": 37.1535635, \"sol_ms\": 8.6875375, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}, {\"uuid\": \"a6c812e5-eb06-5abe-a527-84583b7e08ba\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 4.316672500584138, \"ref_ms\": 7.2327855, \"sol_ms\": 1.6755465, \"max_abs\": 0.03125, \"max_rel\": 0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.315135988894236, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"FIRST WORKING CANDIDATE. 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.3151x. Confirms the list-comprehension root cause and the H1 fusion hypothesis. max_abs 0.03125 within per-workload atol margins at match_ratio 0.98/0.99; max_rel ~0.0078 << 0.05. New baseline/best. Next: perf tuning (Design B row-blocking to cut atomic contention on grad_rw/grad_nw; BLOCK/num_warps sweep), one change per candidate.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 6, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 6 of 100 budget; first valid candidate, geomean 4.3151x\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c007\", \"parent\": \"c006\", \"source_hash\": \"587df6bf53af282adfcc117eabb8145fdd76a252430e58d7f7286dfb55566fca\", \"design\": \"Single-pass, fully H-resident rewrite: grid=rows, BLOCK_H=next_pow2(H)=4096 masked, num_warps=16. Each heavy vector (h0/h1/h2, gc0/1/2, activated, norm_weight, rw0/1/2) loaded EXACTLY ONCE; all H-reductions (var_p/var_c, router dots, g_acoef, g_flat, mbar_c/mbar_p) computed on the resident vectors; then grad_rw/grad_nw atomics and stores in the same program. No list comprehensions (all named scalars). Contrasts c006 which re-read tensors across 4 tiled passes. num_warps=16 keeps per-thread reg count under the c001 overflow point at BLOCK_H=4096.\", \"hypothesis\": \"H(single-pass): eliminating the 3-4x