}], \"geomean_speedup\": 4.609948936385272, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"IMPROVED over c006: 5/5 PASSED, geomean 4.6099x vs 4.3151x (+6.8%). Single-pass read-once confirms the redundant-re-read hypothesis. Same numerics (max_abs 0.03125, max_rel ~0.0078). New best. Note: BLOCK_H=4096 masked wastes ~44% lanes (H=2304); next c008 tries num_warps sweep (8) and/or exact register tuning; a later candidate can try Design B row-blocking to cut grad_rw/grad_nw atomic contention on the 39232-row workload.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 7, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 7 of 100 budget; new best geomean 4.6099x\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c008\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_hash\": \"f9b28ae987e6c072e875ceb03ddb96a22cab0ffdbb419780332e72015ec6be6c\", \"design\": \"Design B row-blocking: grid=cdiv(rows,BLOCK_ROWS) with BLOCK_ROWS=8, BLOCK_H=4096 masked, num_warps=16. Each program owns 8 consecutive rows; router_weight/norm_weight and the 27+9 coef scalars loaded ONCE per program; grad_router[3,H], grad_norm[H], grad_pcw[9,3], grad_ccw[3,3] accumulated in local fp32 registers/SRAM across the 8 rows and flushed with a SINGLE atomic set per program (~8x fewer atomics). Per-row math is the c007 single-pass H-resident body. row<rows guard via lmask. No list comprehensions.\", \"hypothesis\": \"H4 atomics: amortizing grad_rw/grad_nw atomics across 8 rows + loading shared weights once cuts atomic contention (esp. on the 39232-row workload) and improves geomean\", \"change_from_parent\": \"single-row single-pass -> 8-row-blocked program with local accumulation + single atomic flush; grid shrinks 8x\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"per-row math identical to c007 (verified); local accumulators sum correctly across rows (grad_rw/grad_nw/gpcw/gccw are pure sums over rows); lmask=m&(row<rows) prevents OOB and contributes 0 to accumulators for tail rows; idx-subtraction ordering and g_flat index order preserved\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"bases (k