0.0078125}], \"geomean_speedup\": 10.549597332314857, \"all_pass\": true, \"decision\": \"revert\", \"reason\": \"REGRESSION vs c012: geomean 10.5496x < 12.0211x (-12%). Correct (5/5) but slower. At num_warps=8 the BR knee stays at 16, not 8 - BR=8 halves per-program amortization of the grad_rw/grad_nw atomic flush and shared-weight reload, and the extra programs don't help since 108 SMs are already saturated at BR=16 for 4/5 workloads. Confirms c012 (BR=16, nw=8) is the joint optimum of the two config knobs. Sweep summary at nw=8: BR=8->10.55, BR=16->12.02(BEST). Revert to c012. Config knobs (BLOCK_ROWS, num_warps) now jointly exhausted around 12.0x.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 13, \"cumulative_eval_attempts\": 14, \"skills_used\": [], \"tokens_note\": \"eval 13 (attempt 14); c012 remains best at 12.0211x\"}","+{\"candidate\": \"c015\", \"parent\": \"c012\", \"source_hash\": \"40f50d85bdcb27890018ff9510cf05078e2c5167622f6cc59097d354fa65ae61\", \"design\": \"Design B row-blocking, identical kernel/math to c012 (BR=16, BLOCK_H=4096, num_warps=8); only the per-program row loop changed from plain `range(BLOCK_ROWS)` to `tl.range(BLOCK_ROWS, num_stages=2)` to software-pipeline the row iterations (overlap next row's HBM loads with current row's compute).\", \"hypothesis\": \"software-pipelining the row loop (num_stages=2) overlaps load latency with compute and improves throughput on the memory-bound kernel\", \"change_from_parent\": \"row loop range -> tl.range(..., num_stages=2) (pipelining hint; math identical)\", \"validation\": {\"analytic_checks\": \"kernel math identical to c012 (verified); pipelining is a scheduling hint only, results unchanged; local accumulators still summed across all rows\", \"shape_dtype_audit\": \"unchanged; PASSED on evaluator\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"fcd64c92-9a71-592e-ab33-71843be9270f\", \"B\": 64, \"S\": 613, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"pass\": true, \"speedup\": 13.5026, \"ref_ms\": 88.068676, \"sol_ms\": 6.522328, \"max_abs\": 0